it exchanges with node2 on the shared 'seg' L2 segment to node3, using a GRETAP tunnel from node1 to node3 combined with tc/flower filters (ingress and egress, matched on node2's IP, plus ARP) that mirror matching frames into the tunnel. node3 decapsulates via a matching gretap interface (mirr0) and a capture there shows the original node1<->node2 packets, still addressed to each other and not to node3. node1<->node2 traffic itself continues unaffected (verified 0% ping loss throughout, before and after all restarts). Configuration was made persistent via systemd oneshot services on node1 and node3, and static seg-network IPs were made persistent (ifupdown on node1, NetworkManager on node2/node3). All three nodes were restarted one at a time per the mandatory protocol; boot IDs were proven to change on each restart, and after each restart the mirror setup was verified to recover (a bug in the persistence script's qdisc-existence check surfaced after node1's first restart, was fixed, and re-verified working end-to-end; node3's restart later exercised the corrected script cleanly on first try).\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 (SONiC/Debian trixie), node2 and node3 (RHEL9.8) topology; confirmed all three share the isolated 'seg' network (dhcp=false, egress=false) via node1:eth1, node2:enp8s0, node3:enp8s0\",\"Assigned persistent static IPs on the seg segment: node1 eth1=192.168.50.1/24 (via /etc/network/interfaces.d/eth1), node2 enp8s0=192.168.50.2/24 and node3 enp8s0=192.168.50.3/24 (via NetworkManager 'Wired connection 2' profiles)\",\"Installed tcpdump on node2/node3\",\"Captured pre-mirroring baseline: ping node1->node2 succeeded while a simultaneous tcpdump on node3's enp8s0 captured 0 packets, proving the segment is switched (not a hub) and traffic isn't naturally visible to node3\",\"Attempted native Linux ERSPAN tunnel (ip link type erspan) between node1 and node3; found it consistently fails with EINVAL on this kernel across many parameter combinations with no kernel log emitted\",\"Fell back to a GRETAP tunnel (mirr0) between node1 (192.168.50.1) and node3 (192.168.50.3), confirmed link creation succeeds\",\"Configured tc clsact qdisc + flower filters on node1's eth1: ingress src_ip=node2 and egress dst_ip=node2 (covers both ping directions) plus ingress ARP, all with action mirred egress mirror dev mirr0\",\"Verified mirroring end-to-end: ping node1<->node2 succeeded with 0% loss while tcpdump on node3's mirr0 captured all 8 ICMP packets, addressed between node1 and node2's IPs, not node3\",\"Persisted configuration via systemd oneshot units 'seg-mirror.service' on node1 (recreates mirr0 + tc filters) and node3 (recreates mirr0), enabled for multi-user.target\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot IDs, service/interface state) on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node1 via systemd reboot; polled until reachable; confirmed boot ID changed (8e8823ec->a22699da)\",\"Found seg-mirror.service failed on node1 post-restart due to a flawed idempotency check ('tc qdisc show dev eth1 clsact' returning 0 even without a clsact qdisc present); fixed the script to unconditionally add clsact, restarted the service, and re-verified mirroring worked end-to-end again\",\"Restarted node2 via systemd reboot; polled until reachable; confirmed boot ID changed (6bb7e004->43a4b008); verified enp8s0 IP and ping to node1 recovered\",\"Restarted node3 via systemd reboot; polled until reachable; confirmed boot ID changed (bf4e9cbb->0ee30735); verified seg-mirror.service active and mirr0 recreated cleanly on first attempt (using the corrected script)\",\"Ran a final full end-to-end verification after all three restarts: ping node1<->node2 (0% loss) with simultaneous tcpdump on node3's mirr0 capturing all 8 mirrored ICMP packets\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1<->node2 traffic keeps flowing unaffected while mirroring is active\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d701f5625a7e466a\",\"cmd-eb46e101c9984fef\",\"cmd-225d5793c5ea4deb\",\"cmd-cbf13745ba7c4ce1\"],\"summary\":\"Ping from node1 to node2 over the seg interfaces shows 0% packet loss both before mirroring was configured and repeatedly afterward, including after all three node restarts.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-mirroring baseline: node3 does not naturally see node1<->node2 traffic (proves segment is switched, motivates need for mirroring)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a80111e7d5ba4f4e\",\"cmd-21cf728561e8451d\",\"cmd-f9a2a640f90b469f\"],\"summary\":\"tcpdump on node3's enp8s0 during a node1->node2 ping captured 0 packets.\"},{\"requirement\":\"A capture on node3 shows node1<->node2 traffic, addressed elsewhere, once mirroring is configured\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fb653567d6ad486e\",\"cmd-eb46e101c9984fef\",\"cmd-b9036d21e8d1489a\"],\"summary\":\"tcpdump on node3's mirr0 (gretap decap interface) captured all 8 ICMP packets between 192.168.50.1 (node1) and 192.168.50.2 (node2), not addressed to node3.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mirror mechanism configuration (GRETAP tunnel + tc flower filters) on node1 and node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-025649c386a04540\",\"cmd-0ba6e29ef93d4107\",\"cmd-3d6d624bed624c9c\"],\"summary\":\"mirr0 gretap link created and up on both node1 and node3; tc clsact filters on node1's eth1 mirroring ingress/egress traffic matched on node2's IP (plus ARP) into mirr0.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline captured on every node (boot identity, service/interface state)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8183a57819254bb6\",\"cmd-825f4e382b8b4784\",\"cmd-afe129f6f0034649\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id, seg-mirror.service state, and seg interface/mirr0 state on node1, node2, node3 prior to any restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: acknowledgement returns, boot identity changes, service/mirroring recovers\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4139dd542b2c42a0\",\"cmd-76e8a86ea89e40a2\",\"cmd-5c763875f8d94f91\",\"cmd-4b5c1c51ae5d4399\",\"cmd-8e46fed05b274879\",\"cmd-0125e7f84da94391\",\"cmd-4e2808297cef4f6b\"],\"summary\":\"systemd reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; boot_id changed 8e8823ec->a22699da; seg-mirror.service initially failed (journalctl showed 'Parent Qdisc doesn't exists' due to a flawed idempotency check),
...[TRUNCATED 168 CHARACTERS]...
rns, boot identity changes, seg connectivity recovers\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-dd49447f88f84f68\",\"cmd-c52cfe6b17cb4ec1\",\"cmd-8f54087a5c4142b3\"],\"summary\":\"systemd reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed 6bb7e004->43a4b008; enp8s0 seg IP present and ping to node1 succeeded (0% loss) post-restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: acknowledgement returns, boot identity changes, mirror receiver recovers\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4967982a3df2426d\",\"cmd-629b3d9789234ee7\",\"cmd-93a0c352838740c2\",\"cmd-7cb3a5bfad294844\",\"cmd-cbf13745ba7c4ce1\",\"cmd-0ee89a53fef64871\"],\"summary\":\"systemd reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed bf4e9cbb->0ee30735; seg-mirror.service active and mirr0 recreated automatically; final end-to-end test confirmed node3's tcpdump on mirr0 again captured node1<->node2 ping traffic while the ping itself had 0% loss.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to mirror the traffic it exchanges with node2 on the shared 'seg' L2 segment to node3, using a GRETAP tunnel from node1 to node3 combined with tc/flower filters (ingress and egress, matched on node2's IP, plus ARP) that mirror matching frames into the tunnel. node3 decapsulates via a matching gretap interface (mirr0) and a capture there shows the original node1<->node2 packets, still addressed to each other and not to node3. node1<->node2 traffic itself continues unaffected (verified 0% ping loss throughout, before and after all restarts). Configuration was made persistent via systemd oneshot services on node1 and node3, and static seg-network IPs were made persistent (ifupdown on node1, NetworkManager on node2/node3). All three nodes were restarted one at a time per the mandatory protocol; boot IDs were proven to change on each restart, and after each restart the mirror setup was verified to recover (a bug in the persistence script's qdisc-existence check surfaced after node1's first restart, was fixed, and re-verified working end-to-end; node3's restart later exercised the corrected script cleanly on first try).","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 (SONiC/Debian trixie), node2 and node3 (RHEL9.8) topology; confirmed all three share the isolated 'seg' network (dhcp=false, egress=false) via node1:eth1, node2:enp8s0, node3:enp8s0","Assigned persistent static IPs on the seg segment: node1 eth1=192.168.50.1/24 (via /etc/network/interfaces.d/eth1), node2 enp8s0=192.168.50.2/24 and node3 enp8s0=192.168.50.3/24 (via NetworkManager 'Wired connection 2' profiles)","Installed tcpdump on node2/node3","Captured pre-mirroring baseline: ping node1->node2 succeeded while a simultaneous tcpdump on node3's enp8s0 captured 0 packets, proving the segment is switched (not a hub) and traffic isn't naturally visible to node3","Attempted native Linux ERSPAN tunnel (ip link type erspan) between node1 and node3; found it consistently fails with EINVAL on this kernel across many parameter combinations with no kernel log emitted","Fell back to a GRETAP tunnel (mirr0) between node1 (192.168.50.1) and node3 (192.168.50.3), confirmed link creation succeeds","Configured tc clsact qdisc + flower filters on node1's eth1: ingress src_ip=node2 and egress dst_ip=node2 (covers both ping directions) plus ingress ARP, all with action mirred egress mirror dev mirr0","Verified mirroring end-to-end: ping node1<->node2 succeeded with 0% loss while tcpdump on node3's mirr0 captured all 8 ICMP packets, addressed between node1 and node2's IPs, not node3","Persisted configuration via systemd oneshot units 'seg-mirror.service' on node1 (recreates mirr0 + tc filters) and node3 (recreates mirr0), enabled for multi-user.target","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot IDs, service/interface state) on all three nodes","Restarted node1 via systemd reboot; polled until reachable; confirmed boot ID changed (8e8823ec->a22699da)","Found seg-mirror.service failed on node1 post-restart due to a flawed idempotency check ('tc qdisc show dev eth1 clsact' returning 0 even without a clsact qdisc present); fixed the script to unconditionally add clsact, restarted the service, and re-verified mirroring worked end-to-end again","Restarted node2 via systemd reboot; polled until reachable; confirmed boot ID changed (6bb7e004->43a4b008); verified enp8s0 IP and ping to node1 recovered","Restarted node3 via systemd reboot; polled until reachable; confirmed boot ID changed (bf4e9cbb->0ee30735); verified seg-mirror.service active and mirr0 recreated cleanly on first attempt (using the corrected script)","Ran a final full end-to-end verification after all three restarts: ping node1<->node2 (0% loss) with simultaneous tcpdump on node3's mirr0 capturing all 8 mirrored ICMP packets"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1<->node2 traffic keeps flowing unaffected while mirroring is active","command_ids":["cmd-d701f5625a7e466a","cmd-eb46e101c9984fef","cmd-225d5793c5ea4deb","cmd-cbf13745ba7c4ce1"],"summary":"Ping from node1 to node2 over the seg interfaces shows 0% packet loss both before mirroring was configured and repeatedly afterward, including after all three node restarts."},{"requirement":"Pre-mirroring baseline: node3 does not naturally see node1<->node2 traffic (proves segment is switched, motivates need for mirroring)","command_ids":["cmd-a80111e7d5ba4f4e","cmd-21cf728561e8451d","cmd-f9a2a640f90b469f"],"summary":"tcpdump on node3's enp8s0 during a node1->node2 ping captured 0 packets."},{"requirement":"A capture on node3 shows node1<->node2 traffic, addressed elsewhere, once mirroring is configured","command_ids":["cmd-fb653567d6ad486e","cmd-eb46e101c9984fef","cmd-b9036d21e8d1489a"],"summary":"tcpdump on node3's mirr0 (gretap decap interface) captured all 8 ICMP packets between 192.168.50.1 (node1) and 192.168.50.2 (node2), not addressed to node3."},{"requirement":"Mirror mechanism configuration (GRETAP tunnel + tc flower filters) on node1 and node3","command_ids":["cmd-025649c386a04540","cmd-0ba6e29ef93d4107","cmd-3d6d624bed624c9c"],"summary":"mirr0 gretap link created and up on both node1 and node3; tc clsact filters on node1's eth1 mirroring ingress/egress traffic matched on node2's IP (plus ARP) into mirr0."},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline captured on every node (boot identity, service/interface state)","command_ids":["cmd-8183a57819254bb6","cmd-825f4e382b8b4784","cmd-afe129f6f0034649"],"summary":"Captured boot_id, seg-mirror.service state, and seg interface/mirr0 state on node1, node2, node3 prior to any restart."},{"requirement":"node1 restart: acknowledgement returns, boot identity changes, service/mirroring recovers","command_ids":["cmd-4139dd542b2c42a0","cmd-76e8a86ea89e40a2","cmd-5c763875f8d94f91","cmd-4b5c1c51ae5d4399","cmd-8e46fed05b274879","cmd-0125e7f84da94391","cmd-4e2808297cef4f6b"],"summary":"systemd reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; boot_id changed 8e8823ec->a22699da; seg-mirror.service initially failed (journalctl showed 'Parent Qdisc doesn't exists' due to a flawed idempotency check), script was fixed and restarted, and end-to-end mirroring was re-verified working via ping + tcpdump on node3."},{"requirement":"node2 restart: acknowledgement returns, boot identity changes, seg connectivity recovers","command_ids":["cmd-dd49447f88f84f68","cmd-c52cfe6b17cb4ec1","cmd-8f54087a5c4142b3"],"summary":"systemd reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed 6bb7e004->43a4b008; enp8s0 seg IP present and ping to node1 succeeded (0% loss) post-restart."},{"requirement":"node3 restart: acknowledgement returns, boot identity changes, mirror receiver recovers","command_ids":["cmd-4967982a3df2426d","cmd-629b3d9789234ee7","cmd-93a0c352838740c2","cmd-7cb3a5bfad294844","cmd-cbf13745ba7c4ce1","cmd-0ee89a53fef64871"],"summary":"systemd reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed bf4e9cbb->0ee30735; seg-mirror.service active and mirr0 recreated automatically; final end-to-end test confirmed node3's tcpdump on mirr0 again captured node1<->node2 ping traffic while the ping itself had 0% loss."}]},"ttf